01:40:44.642 --> 01:40:46.642
that is the lowest virtue.

762
01:40:46.642 --> 01:40:51.642
Pride and arrogance ruin everything in your life.

763
01:40:51.642 --> 01:40:54.642
He wants you to be humble.

764
01:40:54.642 --> 01:40:57.642
So when that person comes to church,

765
01:40:57.642 --> 01:40:59.642
and they are not doing well,

766
01:40:59.642 --> 01:41:02.642
and they are still cursing at the coffee,

767
01:41:02.642 --> 01:41:05.642
or they still smell a bit like last night's beer,

768
01:41:05.642 --> 01:41:06.642
who cares.

769
01:41:06.642 --> 01:41:08.642
He has set you free as well.

770
01:41:08.642 --> 01:41:11.642
And now He is working with him.

771
01:41:11.642 --> 01:41:14.642
And in that humility we must be humble,

772
01:41:14.642 --> 01:41:17.642
to be able to take that person along in love.

773
01:41:17.642 --> 01:41:20.642
So what Paul is doing here,

774
01:41:20.642 --> 01:41:23.642
is he is rewarding someone,

775
01:41:23.642 --> 01:41:25.642
that when you are doing well,

776
01:41:25.642 --> 01:41:27.642
and when you can quote Scripture,

777
01:41:27.642 --> 01:41:30.642
and when you come to church every Sunday,

778
01:41:30.642 --> 01:41:33.642
and when you have cleaned up all sorts of filth and uncleanness,

779
01:41:33.642 --> 01:41:35.642
then there is now the next instruction,

780
01:41:35.642 --> 01:41:38.642
be then for love and humility.

781
01:41:38.642 --> 01:41:40.642
And know what you owe it to.

782
01:41:40.642 --> 01:41:43.642
It is not from your years of investing,

783
01:41:43.642 --> 01:41:45.642
that you have read your little Bible every day,

784
01:41:45.642 --> 01:41:46.642
that you are doing so well,

785
01:41:46.642 --> 01:41:49.642
even though you have to read your Bible every day for days on end.

786
01:41:49.642 --> 01:41:54.642
No, everything is the glory of the grace of King Jesus.

787
01:41:54.642 --> 01:41:58.642
We owe it all to Him.

788
01:41:58.642 --> 01:42:01.642
And this must remain in us.

789
01:42:01.642 --> 01:42:03.642
And when I was thinking about this,

790
01:42:03.642 --> 01:42:05.642
and when I was working on this sermon,

791
01:42:05.642 --> 01:42:07.642
I thought, you know what,

792
01:42:07.642 --> 01:42:12.642
I am going to take a number of examples from the Bible,

793
01:42:12.642 --> 01:42:15.642
of stories of humility and lowliness.

794
01:42:15.642 --> 01:42:17.642
And then I quickly realized,

795
01:42:17.642 --> 01:42:18.642
that I am not going to do that,

796
01:42:18.642 --> 01:42:21.642
because there are more than a thousand stories,

797
01:42:21.642 --> 01:42:22.642
that we can go through,

798
01:42:22.642 --> 01:42:28.642
to look at what God truly values as humility.

799
01:42:28.642 --> 01:42:32.642
No, we must stay here in Philippians chapter 2,

800
01:42:32.642 --> 01:42:34.642
verses 6 to 11.

801
01:42:34.642 --> 01:42:35.642
Come with me for a moment,

802
01:42:35.642 --> 01:42:37.642
we're going to do a quick Bible study.

803
01:42:37.642 --> 01:42:42.642
Verse 6, please.

804
01:42:42.642 --> 01:42:47.642
I have six quick lessons on humility for you,

805
01:42:47.642 --> 01:42:50.642
in the last few minutes, that we will share together.

806
01:42:50.642 --> 01:42:53.642
Lesson 1, if you're taking notes,

807
01:42:53.642 --> 01:42:57.642
being humble, lesson 1 we can find in verse 6,

808
01:42:57.642 --> 01:43:01.642
is to place God above you.

809
01:43:01.642 --> 01:43:04.642
Place God above you.

810
01:43:04.642 --> 01:43:06.642
Lesson 1 in verse 6.

811
01:43:06.642 --> 01:43:08.642
Jesus was God,

812
01:43:08.642 --> 01:43:11.642
but he didn't consider that so important,

813
01:43:11.642 --> 01:43:13.642
that he couldn't let it go.

814
01:43:13.642 --> 01:43:16.642
And now we need to make a strange turn,

815
01:43:16.642 --> 01:43:18.642
because Jesus himself was the highest,

816
01:43:18.642 --> 01:43:21.642
that’s why he is also the best example of humility.

817
01:43:21.642 --> 01:43:23.642
I can bring up Moses,

818
01:43:23.642 --> 01:43:26.642
I can bring up all sorts of people in the Bible,

819
01:43:26.642 --> 01:43:28.642
who were very humble,

820
01:43:28.642 --> 01:43:30.642
but Jesus is the greatest example, amen?

821
01:43:30.642 --> 01:43:32.642
He was God Himself,

822
01:43:32.642 --> 01:43:36.642
but he didn't find that so important,

823
01:43:36.642 --> 01:43:38.642
that he couldn't let it go.

824
01:43:39.642 --> 01:43:43.642
Dear people in the church, let go.

825
01:43:43.642 --> 01:43:48.642
Let go of that one thing that holds you.

826
01:43:48.642 --> 01:43:51.642
For things do not hold you,

827
01:43:51.642 --> 01:43:55.642
you hold onto things.

828
01:43:55.642 --> 01:43:59.642
Very often people blame Satan for everything,

829
01:43:59.642 --> 01:44:02.642
and Satan does this to me, and Satan does that to me,

830
01:44:02.642 --> 01:44:07.642
but you should know how much authority you have yourself.

831
01:44:07.642 --> 01:44:11.642
And most of the things you are struggling with,

832
01:44:11.642 --> 01:44:13.642
it's not that Satan has you trapped,

833
01:44:13.642 --> 01:44:16.642
but that you are holding onto Satan.

834
01:44:16.642 --> 01:44:21.642
Because you want to find control in that forgiveness,

835
01:44:21.642 --> 01:44:25.642
towards your brother, or your sister, or your parent, or your uncle,

836
01:44:25.642 --> 01:44:28.642
or that person in the church. Let go.

837
01:44:28.642 --> 01:44:30.642
Yes, but I need this and that,

838
01:44:30.642 --> 01:44:33.642
and that's why I go back every time, that's my go-to drug.

839
01:44:33.642 --> 01:44:35.642
Let go.

840
01:44:35.642 --> 01:44:38.642
God who says, you can let it go.

841
01:44:38.642 --> 01:44:40.642
But as long as you hold on to it,

842
01:44:40.642 --> 01:44:45.642
you position yourself as the one who holds on.

843
01:44:45.642 --> 01:44:47.642
Hence that free will.

844
01:44:47.642 --> 01:44:51.642
No one in this church can say, I cannot.

845
01:44:51.642 --> 01:44:53.642
For through the blood of King Jesus,

846
01:44:53.642 --> 01:44:56.642
you are more than a conqueror.

847
01:44:56.642 --> 01:45:01.642
So go ahead and challenge me, but I cannot.

848
01:45:01.642 --> 01:45:05.642
For here stands a lot of misery, and I could too.

849
01:45:05.642 --> 01:45:07.642
Through Jesus.

850
01:45:07.642 --> 01:45:10.642
So you must place God above you.

851
01:45:10.642 --> 01:45:13.642
You must know that there is someone who is higher than you.

852
01:45:13.642 --> 01:45:16.642
You must know that there is someone who is stronger than you.

853
01:45:16.642 --> 01:45:19.642
You must know that you must give an account

854
01:45:19.642 --> 01:45:21.642
to the one who is above you.

855
01:45:21.642 --> 01:45:23.642
His name is God.

856
01:45:23.642 --> 01:45:25.642
He is the Most High.

857
01:45:25.642 --> 01:45:27.642
And we will have to give an account to him.

858
01:45:27.642 --> 01:45:31.642
And instead of just being in that debt towards him,

859
01:45:31.642 --> 01:45:37.642
he gives us the way out through his Son, Jesus Christ.

860
01:45:37.642 --> 01:45:41.642
This week I was watching a debate between a Muslim and a Christian.

861
01:45:41.642 --> 01:45:47.642
And that Muslim who says, nowhere does Jesus say that he is God.

862
01:45:47.642 --> 01:45:52.642
And then I always think to myself, bring it on!

863
01:45:52.642 --> 01:45:54.642
Because I want to engage in that debate.

864
01:45:54.642 --> 01:45:57.642
Jesus continuously says that he is God.

865
01:45:57.642 --> 01:46:00.642
He constantly makes ego-amy claims.

866
01:46:00.642 --> 01:46:06.642
But then I would say to that gentleman the Muslim, that's correct.

867
01:46:06.642 --> 01:46:10.642
Jesus never says about himself, I am God.

868
01:46:10.642 --> 01:46:15.642
Because in Philippians chapter 2, verse 6 it says, he was himself God.

869
01:46:15.642 --> 01:46:17.642
Prove that he was God.

870
01:46:17.642 --> 01:46:23.642
But he did not find it so important that he wanted to hold on to his divinity.

871
01:46:23.642 --> 01:46:25.642
But he wanted to let it go.

872
01:46:25.642 --> 01:46:33.642
So as long as Jesus walked the earth, he did not hold on to his divinity.

873
01:46:33.642 --> 01:46:38.642
That makes him indeed the Lord of lords.

874
01:46:38.642 --> 01:46:44.642
So when someone comes to Jesus and says, good master, good master.

875
01:46:44.642 --> 01:46:46.642
Do you know what Jesus then says?

876
01:46:46.642 --> 01:46:49.642
Do not call me good, only God is good.

877
01:46:49.642 --> 01:46:54.642
In other words, Jesus places God above himself, while he was fully human.

878
01:46:54.642 --> 01:46:59.642
Really, verses 6 to 11 are more brilliant when you think about it.

879
01:46:59.642 --> 01:47:03.642
Jesus continuously places God above himself.

880
01:47:03.642 --> 01:47:07.642
I can do nothing unless I see the Father do it.

881
01:47:07.642 --> 01:47:09.642
I and the Father are one.

882
01:47:09.642 --> 01:47:11.642
I only do what the Father does.

883
01:47:11.642 --> 01:47:16.642
Lord, if it is possible, may this cup pass from me.

884
01:47:16.642 --> 01:47:19.642
But not my will, but Your will be done.

885
01:47:19.642 --> 01:47:24.642
So Jesus was continuously busy setting an example for humanity.

886
01:47:24.642 --> 01:47:28.642
Lesson 1, placing God above oneself.

887
01:47:28.642 --> 01:47:29.642
Amen?

888
01:47:29.642 --> 01:47:35.642
Verse 7, humility is servanthood.

889
01:47:35.642 --> 01:47:39.642
If you are taking notes, the first was to place God above you.

890
01:47:39.642 --> 01:47:42.642
The second is servanthood.

891
01:47:43.642 --> 01:47:46.642
No, He even laid aside all His divinity.

892
01:47:46.642 --> 01:47:49.642
He came to earth to become what?

893
01:47:49.642 --> 01:47:51.642
To become a servant.

894
01:47:51.642 --> 01:47:53.642
He became fully human.

895
01:47:53.642 --> 01:47:55.642
A servant.

896
01:47:55.642 --> 01:47:59.642
Can you imagine that Jesus, Creator of heaven and earth,

897
01:47:59.642 --> 01:48:02.642
Jesus who gave the law through Moses,

898
01:48:02.642 --> 01:48:04.642
it was Jesus who gave the law to Moses,

899
01:48:04.642 --> 01:48:08.642
Jesus who gave that law to Moses, with all those purification laws,

900
01:48:08.642 --> 01:48:11.642
all those ceremonial laws, it was Jesus Himself.

901
01:48:11.642 --> 01:48:15.642
who said to the people of Israel, you are my pure people,

902
01:48:15.642 --> 01:48:17.642
you belong to me.

903
01:48:17.642 --> 01:48:21.642
It is Jesus himself who then kneels down

904
01:48:21.642 --> 01:48:24.642
to wash the feet of his disciples.

905
01:48:24.642 --> 01:48:30.642
To which Peter protests very strongly, this cannot happen.

906
01:48:30.642 --> 01:48:33.642
Why? That was the lowest of the low.

907
01:48:33.642 --> 01:48:35.642
Washing someone's feet.

908
01:48:35.642 --> 01:48:39.642
Middle East, open soles, you walk there,

909
01:48:39.642 --> 01:48:43.642
a lot of sand under your toenails, all of it.

910
01:48:43.642 --> 01:48:47.642
And then you come into someone's house, and what does Jesus do?

911
01:48:47.642 --> 01:48:52.642
He himself, the rabbi himself, the highest of his group of disciples,

912
01:48:52.642 --> 01:48:55.642
goes himself to wash the feet of his disciples.

913
01:48:55.642 --> 01:48:59.642
Peter protests with everything that is in him.

914
01:48:59.642 --> 01:49:02.642
In The Chosen, season 5, so well done.

915
01:49:02.642 --> 01:49:05.642
Do you all know The Chosen actually?

916
01:49:05.642 --> 01:49:08.642
Yes? You really have to watch it, mandatory.

917
01:49:08.642 --> 01:49:11.642
And then Peter says, no, this is not going to happen.

918
01:49:11.642 --> 01:49:15.642
And then Jesus says, then you have nothing to do with me.

919
01:49:15.642 --> 01:49:19.642
And then Peter says, then I want you to wash me completely.

920
01:49:19.642 --> 01:49:22.642
So cool, so cool.

921
01:49:22.642 --> 01:49:25.642
The other thing I have written down,

922
01:49:25.642 --> 01:49:29.642
is an instruction to all my brothers and sisters in open church,

923
01:49:29.642 --> 01:49:32.642
who may have been raised Protestant or Catholic.

924
01:49:32.642 --> 01:49:35.642
My dear sister who is sitting over there,

925
01:49:35.642 --> 01:49:38.642
who passed by on her bike, with a Catholic background.

926
01:49:38.642 --> 01:49:42.642
There are many in open church who have a Catholic background.

927
01:49:42.642 --> 01:49:45.642
And I want to say something about humility.

928
01:49:45.642 --> 01:49:51.642
Jesus steps into the water with John the Baptist,

929
01:49:51.642 --> 01:49:56.642
and Jesus, as an adult man, steps into the water with John the Baptist,

930
01:49:56.642 --> 01:50:00.642
and he says to John, I want you to baptize me.

931
01:50:00.642 --> 01:50:09.642
And John replies, no, no, I should not baptize you, you should baptize me.

932
01:50:09.642 --> 01:50:12.642
And do you know what Jesus then says?

933
01:50:12.642 --> 01:50:19.642
Just baptize me, John, to fully obey righteousness.

934
01:50:20.642 --> 01:50:24.642
Then I will have a party just on this stage.

935
01:50:24.642 --> 01:50:27.642
I find that so profound.

936
01:50:27.642 --> 01:50:30.642
For Jesus, he who was without sin,

937
01:50:30.642 --> 01:50:33.642
Jesus who is the Almighty,

938
01:50:33.642 --> 01:50:36.642
Jesus who shines,

939
01:50:36.642 --> 01:50:39.642
Jesus who has done nothing wrong,

940
01:50:39.642 --> 01:50:42.642
could indeed fully say,

941
01:50:42.642 --> 01:50:46.642
Yes, you are actually right about that, Johannes, I actually need to baptize you.

942
01:50:46.642 --> 01:50:49.642
But then he would have lost immediately.

943
01:50:49.642 --> 01:50:52.642
And instead of Jesus,

944
01:50:52.642 --> 01:50:55.642
while he was completely pure and holy,

945
01:50:55.642 --> 01:50:58.642
instead of standing his ground,

946
01:50:58.642 --> 01:51:01.642
and saying, okay, I baptize you.

947
01:51:01.642 --> 01:51:04.642
I don't know why I'm speaking English, but anyway.

948
01:51:04.642 --> 01:51:07.642
Instead of that, Jesus says,

949
01:51:07.642 --> 01:51:10.642
I want to be obedient to what God the Father says.

950
01:51:10.642 --> 01:51:13.642
And I will do that.

951
01:51:13.642 --> 01:51:16.642
And dear people in the open church,

952
01:51:16.642 --> 01:51:19.642
if you have already been baptized as a child,

953
01:51:19.642 --> 01:51:22.642
I just leave it at that,

954
01:51:22.642 --> 01:51:25.642
if you have already been baptized as a child, and you struggle with those thoughts,

955
01:51:25.642 --> 01:51:28.642
should I be baptized again?

956
01:51:28.642 --> 01:51:31.642
And you think to yourself, I was already baptized as a child, so I think that's it.

957
01:51:31.642 --> 01:51:34.642
My pastoral encouragement is, be humble of heart,

958
01:51:34.642 --> 01:51:37.642
listen to what Jesus said to Johannes,

959
01:51:37.642 --> 01:51:40.642
and then say, in order to fully fulfill righteousness,

960
01:51:40.642 --> 01:51:43.642
I want to be obediently baptized.

961
01:51:43.642 --> 01:51:46.642
Being baptized as an adult person,

962
01:51:46.642 --> 01:51:49.642
is obedience to King Jesus.

963
01:51:49.642 --> 01:51:52.642
That is all I will say about that subject. Obedience.

964
01:51:52.642 --> 01:51:55.642
And so,

965
01:51:55.642 --> 01:51:58.642
Jesus positions Himself

966
01:51:58.642 --> 01:52:01.642
as service to God,

967
01:52:01.642 --> 01:52:04.642
and because He was serving,

968
01:52:04.642 --> 01:52:07.642
He could also do everything for humanity,

969
01:52:07.642 --> 01:52:10.642
even though they spat in His face,

970
01:52:10.642 --> 01:52:13.642
even though they placed a crown on His head,

971
01:52:13.642 --> 01:52:16.642
even though they did not recognize Him,

972
01:52:16.642 --> 01:52:19.642
even though He Himself was a Jew, the Jews did not recognize Him.

973
01:52:19.642 --> 01:52:22.642
So deeply did Jesus have to go, why?

974
01:52:22.642 --> 01:52:25.642
Because He did not come as God Himself,

975
01:52:25.642 --> 01:52:28.642
but He came as a servant.

976
01:52:28.642 --> 01:52:31.642
Lessons in humility 1, putting God above you,

977
01:52:31.642 --> 01:52:34.642
number 2, service,

978
01:52:34.642 --> 01:52:37.642
and as a man He humbled Himself,

979
01:52:37.642 --> 01:52:40.642
humility,

980
01:52:40.642 --> 01:52:43.642
humbled, making yourself lower,

981
01:52:43.642 --> 01:52:46.642
by God, and here is the lesson,

982
01:52:46.642 --> 01:52:49.642
to be obedient unto death.

983
01:52:49.642 --> 01:52:52.642
Lessons in humility 1, to place God above you,

984
01:52:52.642 --> 01:52:55.642
number 2, servanthood,

985
01:52:55.642 --> 01:52:58.642
number 3, obedience.

986
01:52:58.642 --> 01:53:01.642
Humility is obedience.

987
01:53:01.642 --> 01:53:04.642
Humility is reading what Scripture says,

988
01:53:04.642 --> 01:53:07.642
and just doing it.

989
01:53:07.642 --> 01:53:10.642
Humility is not thinking what you read here in the Bible,

990
01:53:10.642 --> 01:53:13.642
yes, but I actually see that differently.

991
01:53:13.642 --> 01:53:16.642
No, humility is knowing that God's Word is the truth,

992
01:53:16.642 --> 01:53:19.642
and even though God's Word clashes with your flesh,

993
01:53:19.642 --> 01:53:22.642
every time, you must not place yourself above Scripture,

994
01:53:22.642 --> 01:53:25.642
but you must humbly position yourself in obedience to Scripture.

995
01:53:25.642 --> 01:53:28.642
That is why Paul

996
01:53:28.642 --> 01:53:31.642
could also sit in a prison to do this,

997
01:53:31.642 --> 01:53:34.642
because he was obedient to what God has to say.

998
01:53:34.642 --> 01:53:37.642
And I want to link that obedience to the concept of leading.

999
01:53:37.642 --> 01:53:40.642
Leading, not with a short 'ei', but with a long 'ei'.

1000
01:53:40.642 --> 01:53:43.642
Oh, how we would like to lead with a short 'ei'?

1001
01:53:43.642 --> 01:53:46.642
But that is not humility.

1002
01:53:46.642 --> 01:53:49.642
Suffering with a long 'i' is humility.

1003
01:53:49.642 --> 01:53:52.642
In fact, the Bible says,

1004
01:53:52.642 --> 01:53:55.642
in a dangerous situation,

1005
01:53:55.642 --> 01:53:58.642
that Jesus had to learn obedience.

1006
01:53:58.642 --> 01:54:01.642
And how did he have to learn obedience?

1007
01:54:01.642 --> 01:54:04.642
By suffering.

1008
01:54:04.642 --> 01:54:07.642
So by suffering, you can learn

1009
01:54:07.642 --> 01:54:10.642
to become obedient to God.

1010
01:54:10.642 --> 01:54:13.642
Because, you see, when I tell my son,

1011
01:54:13.642 --> 01:54:16.642
Joshua, please clean up that noodle mess

1012
01:54:16.642 --> 01:54:19.642
that you left in the kitchen.

1013
01:54:19.642 --> 01:54:22.642
I see him, and then I say,

1014
01:54:23.642 --> 01:54:26.642
I see him doing this, because he is a teenager.

1015
01:54:26.642 --> 01:54:29.642
I see him struggling with everything inside him.

1016
01:54:29.642 --> 01:54:32.642
And he doesn't want to do it.

1017
01:54:32.642 --> 01:54:35.642
But then I say, Joshua, you are going to do it now.

1018
01:54:35.642 --> 01:54:38.642
But dad, I have already started this game.

1019
01:54:38.642 --> 01:54:41.642
All the parents here in the room, yes, I understand what you mean.

1020
01:54:41.642 --> 01:54:44.642
I have already started the game. A thousand very good reasons.

1021
01:54:44.642 --> 01:54:47.642
Flimsy excuses. Very good reasons why it cannot happen.

1022
01:54:47.642 --> 01:54:50.642
And then I force him to clean up that kitchen first.

1023
01:54:51.642 --> 01:54:54.642
Because he needs to learn obedience.

1024
01:54:54.642 --> 01:54:57.642
It is of course a miniature that he then has to lead.

1025
01:54:57.642 --> 01:55:00.642
But I say that on purpose. As a miniature.

1026
01:55:00.642 --> 01:55:03.642
That he has to put something down.

1027
01:55:03.642 --> 01:55:06.642
He has to miss something.

1028
01:55:06.642 --> 01:55:12.642
He has to give something up to be obedient to what the Lord says.

1029
01:55:12.642 --> 01:55:15.642
So when you are sitting here in the church,

1030
01:55:15.642 --> 01:55:18.642
and you read God's Word,

1031
01:55:18.642 --> 01:55:21.642
and God's Word clashes against your flesh,

1032
01:55:21.642 --> 01:55:24.642
know that the Holy Spirit is working with you.

1033
01:55:24.642 --> 01:55:28.642
Because this is exactly where God wants you to be.

1034
01:55:28.642 --> 01:55:32.642
Do not be afraid to suffer with a long 'ij'.

1035
01:55:32.642 --> 01:55:35.642
Do not try to escape suffering.

1036
01:55:35.642 --> 01:55:39.642
People who do that, who want to escape suffering,

1037
01:55:39.642 --> 01:55:43.642
will come up with reasons, will come up with excuses,

1038
01:55:43.642 --> 01:55:47.642
will come up with ways out, will cause their own Ishmaels.

1039
01:55:47.642 --> 01:55:52.642
If you want to escape suffering, you will create all sorts of sidetracks.

1040
01:55:52.642 --> 01:55:56.642
And I guarantee you, those sidetracks will not help you.

1041
01:55:56.642 --> 01:56:01.642
All detours to ultimately escape suffering,

1042
01:56:01.642 --> 01:56:04.642
ultimately they return to the same point again.

1043
01:56:04.642 --> 01:56:07.642
Do you know why? Because God wants to teach you something.

1044
01:56:07.642 --> 01:56:11.642
If you haven't learned that lesson, He wants to present it to you once more.

1045
01:56:11.642 --> 01:56:15.642
And so, fourteen days through the desert can become forty years.

1046
01:56:15.642 --> 01:56:18.642
For in the end, you will learn what you need to learn.

1047
01:56:18.642 --> 01:56:22.642
So therefore embrace, I had just written here,

1048
01:56:22.642 --> 01:56:25.642
embrace the concept of suffering.

1049
01:56:25.642 --> 01:56:29.642
That is why Randolph and Maureen are such a great example for us.

1050
01:56:29.642 --> 01:56:33.642
That is why all the people in Open Church who have lost a loved one,

1051
01:56:33.642 --> 01:56:36.642
who still believe in King Jesus and say

1052
01:56:36.642 --> 01:56:38.642
I will continue to come to Jesus.

1053
01:56:38.642 --> 01:56:42.642
You are a very great example for the other people.

1054
01:56:43.642 --> 01:56:47.642
The last two lessons. I find these very important.

1055
01:56:47.642 --> 01:56:49.642
I find them all important.

1056
01:56:49.642 --> 01:56:53.642
Let's read verse 9 together. Verse 9.

1057
01:56:53.642 --> 01:56:59.642
So because Jesus did what He did,

1058
01:56:59.642 --> 01:57:04.642
precisely because He was so humble, verse 9,

1059
01:57:04.642 --> 01:57:10.642
therefore God has also given Him the highest honor and the utmost power.

1060
01:57:10.642 --> 01:57:16.642
He has made Him more important and more powerful than anyone.

1061
01:57:16.642 --> 01:57:18.642
The lesson I have written down is,

1062
01:57:18.642 --> 01:57:26.642
you must expect your reward from God and also in His time.

1063
01:57:26.642 --> 01:57:30.642
Do not seek your own reward in this life.

1064
01:57:30.642 --> 01:57:33.642
Do not seek your own dignity in this life.

1065
01:57:33.642 --> 01:57:38.642
Do not stand in a certain way so that everyone finds you interesting,

1066
01:57:38.642 --> 01:57:42.642
for then Jesus says, you have already received your reward.

1067
01:57:42.642 --> 01:57:48.642
But wait until God will exalt you, for He will exalt you.

1068
01:57:48.642 --> 01:57:52.642
Vanessa and I have indicated a lot lately as well

1069
01:57:52.642 --> 01:57:56.642
that rewards are not from here and now.

1070
01:57:56.642 --> 01:58:01.642
Honestly, this earth, this life, the 90 years you have been given,

1071
01:58:01.642 --> 01:58:03.642
the age limit is going up a bit,

1072
01:58:03.642 --> 01:58:05.642
but the 90 years you have been given on this earth,

1073
01:58:05.642 --> 01:58:09.642
is not the period to gather rewards.

1074
01:58:09.642 --> 01:58:13.642
God will provide, God will bless,

1075
01:58:13.642 --> 01:58:18.642
but all those provisions and blessings are not rewards yet.

1076
01:58:18.642 --> 01:58:23.642
For provisions are there so that you can gather them,

1077
01:58:23.642 --> 01:58:28.642
so that you can manage the blessings of your life as a good steward.

1078
01:58:28.642 --> 01:58:31.642
If you have a lot of money, that is not just for you,

1079
01:58:31.642 --> 01:58:34.642
that is to be able to bless other people around you.

1080
01:58:34.642 --> 01:58:37.642
If you are very wise, that wisdom is not just for you,

1081
01:58:37.642 --> 01:58:39.642
that is to be able to bless other people.

1082
01:58:39.642 --> 01:58:45.642
So when God blesses and provides, that is not yet the reward of this earth.

1083
01:58:45.642 --> 01:58:47.642
Have you heard what I am saying?

1084
01:58:47.642 --> 01:58:53.642
This earth is not the timeline of reward, yet.

1085
01:58:53.642 --> 01:58:58.642
The Bible clearly says, God has also given His Holy Spirit

1086
01:58:58.642 --> 01:59:05.642
as a foretaste of the reward that awaits you.

1087
01:59:05.642 --> 01:59:08.642
And that is why we have a glorious God.

1088
01:59:08.642 --> 01:59:12.642
For we have millions of people on this earth,

1089
01:59:12.642 --> 01:59:16.642
who are not rich, as we are rich in the western world.

1090
01:59:16.642 --> 01:59:20.642
Sometimes I sit at the table, then I pray with my children,

1091
01:59:20.642 --> 01:59:22.642
then I look at the food they have been able to put together,

1092
01:59:22.642 --> 01:59:25.642
and then I say, Lord, I want to pause here,

1093
01:59:25.642 --> 01:59:29.642
that it is not a given that we can just eat what we eat.

1094
01:59:29.642 --> 01:59:34.642
There are millions of people living below the hunger line.

1095
01:59:34.642 --> 01:59:37.642
What about that? Is that a good God then?

1096
01:59:37.642 --> 01:59:42.642
Those people know that the reward is not in the here and now.

1097
01:59:42.642 --> 01:59:46.642
For the reward will come when we see Him face to face.

1098
01:59:46.642 --> 01:59:49.642
And how you position yourself in this life,

1099
01:59:49.642 --> 01:59:54.642
that determines how great your reward will be when we see Jesus.

1100
01:59:54.642 --> 01:59:57.642
If you accept Jesus, you are saved.

1101
01:59:57.642 --> 02:00:01.642
When you live for Him, humbly positioning yourself,

1102
02:00:01.642 --> 02:00:04.642
and you obey Him, and you even go through suffering,

1103
02:00:04.642 --> 02:00:09.642
then He will be able to bless you with all kinds of rewards when we see Him.

1104
02:00:09.642 --> 02:00:11.642
And I am looking forward to that.

1105
02:00:11.642 --> 02:00:13.642
You may look forward to that.

1106
02:00:13.642 --> 02:00:17.642
So when you sow, you may look forward to a harvest.

1107
02:00:17.642 --> 02:00:21.642
And that harvest is greatest when you are at peace.

1108
02:00:21.642 --> 02:00:24.642
When you expect the harvest from Him.

1109
02:00:24.642 --> 02:00:28.642
And when you expect the harvest from Him in His time.

1110
02:00:28.642 --> 02:00:34.642
Jesus had to die before He received His reward.

1111
02:00:34.642 --> 02:00:40.642
Jesus had not received any rewards at the moment He was here.

1112
02:00:40.642 --> 02:00:46.642
Many people are blessed and healed through the miraculous works of King Jesus.

1113
02:00:47.642 --> 02:00:52.642
But Isaiah says that He was a man of sorrows.

1114
02:00:52.642 --> 02:00:56.642
He was a man of deep disappointment.

1115
02:00:56.642 --> 02:01:01.642
He was a man who went through deep suffering.

1116
02:01:01.642 --> 02:01:04.642
Denied by His own people.

1117
02:01:04.642 --> 02:01:09.642
Mocked, as Randolph just said, by the ten men.

1118
02:01:09.642 --> 02:01:13.642
Of the ten clean lepers, only one came back.

1119
02:01:13.642 --> 02:01:16.642
How sad is that? That is really sad.

1120
02:01:16.642 --> 02:01:18.642
But Jesus knew.

1121
02:01:18.642 --> 02:01:24.642
The Hebrew letter says, He looked with longing at the cross.

1122
02:01:24.642 --> 02:01:26.642
Knowing what He could gain.

1123
02:01:26.642 --> 02:01:28.642
He could win you with it.

1124
02:01:28.642 --> 02:01:30.642
And that was His prize.

1125
02:01:30.642 --> 02:01:33.642
For He knew if I humbly obey God.

1126
02:01:33.642 --> 02:01:37.642
And I expect His reward in His time.

1127
02:01:37.642 --> 02:01:40.642
Then, verse 9, let's take another look at that together.

1128
02:01:40.642 --> 02:01:46.642
Therefore God has also given Him the highest honor and the utmost power.

1129
02:01:46.642 --> 02:01:52.642
He has made Him more important and more powerful than anyone else.

1130
02:01:52.642 --> 02:01:55.642
The last lesson is this.

1131
02:01:55.642 --> 02:01:58.642
Shall we stand? I want to close the service.

1132
02:01:58.642 --> 02:02:01.642
The last lesson is this.

1133
02:02:03.642 --> 02:02:09.642
Humility means bowing the knee to King Jesus.

1134
02:02:10.642 --> 02:02:12.642
That is humility.

1135
02:02:12.642 --> 02:02:15.642
Bowing the knee to King Jesus.

1136
02:02:15.642 --> 02:02:19.642
Worship is humility.

1137
02:02:19.642 --> 02:02:23.642
Worship is humility.

1138
02:02:23.642 --> 02:02:27.642
Dear church, I say this to all of you.

1139
02:02:29.642 --> 02:02:33.642
Be humble and worship God.

1140
02:02:34.642 --> 02:02:42.642
The Bible says here in this verse, God wants us to bow our knees to King Jesus.

1141
02:02:42.642 --> 02:02:47.642
You can approach it very symbolically, or you do it regularly as well.

1142
02:02:47.642 --> 02:02:51.642
I know there is little space between the chairs and we don't have to do that now.

1143
02:02:51.642 --> 02:02:54.642
For you shouldn't do it just because I'm saying it now.

1144
02:02:54.642 --> 02:03:00.642
But very often when it's Monday evening, or even on a Sunday morning, I get down on my knees.

1145
02:03:01.642 --> 02:03:07.642
Why? Not to act fake humble, but because the Bible says so.

1146
02:03:07.642 --> 02:03:14.642
If you ever find yourself in your bedroom, or you have a certain room where you pray to God, kneel.

1147
02:03:14.642 --> 02:03:17.642
Let me give you this instruction.

1148
02:03:17.642 --> 02:03:19.642
Do you ever do this?

1149
02:03:19.642 --> 02:03:22.642
Do you ever kneel before the Lord?

1150
02:03:22.642 --> 02:03:24.642
This is what God Himself asks.

1151
02:03:24.642 --> 02:03:26.642
It is an instruction from God.

1152
02:03:26.642 --> 02:03:36.642
It says here, for God wants, read that verse with me, for God wants, that is what He wants,

1153
02:03:36.642 --> 02:03:46.642
that everyone in heaven, angels, demons, even Satan, everyone, no one excluded,

1154
02:03:47.642 --> 02:03:56.642
God wants that everyone in heaven, on earth, and under the earth, will bow their knees to Jesus.

1155
02:03:56.642 --> 02:04:05.642
If you want to know what humility is, and if you want to express humility physically, then it is to go on your knees.

1156
02:04:05.642 --> 02:04:11.642
For humility can be expressed emotionally, by giving forgiveness, by acknowledging people,

1157
02:04:11.642 --> 02:04:15.642
by being a good Samaritan, by caring for others.

1158
02:04:15.642 --> 02:04:19.642
Even if they don't look like you, even if they don't believe the same as you do,

1159
02:04:19.642 --> 02:04:24.642
a good Samaritan is someone who humbly helps those around him because he has love.

1160
02:04:24.642 --> 02:04:26.642
In that, you can show God.

1161
02:04:26.642 --> 02:04:32.642
But physical humility, what God asks of us, is that we bow our knees from time to time.

1162
02:04:32.642 --> 02:04:36.642
Do it in your own prayer room. Do it in your own time.

1163
02:04:36.642 --> 02:04:41.642
Get on your knees. Are you having difficulty surrendering yourself to Jesus and saying,

1164
02:04:41.642 --> 02:04:45.642
Lord, I acknowledge you as Lord. I acknowledge you as God.

1165
02:04:45.642 --> 02:04:49.642
For I will tell you, if you do this, you will be blessed.

1166
02:04:49.642 --> 02:04:51.642
That is truly the case.

1167
02:04:51.642 --> 02:04:55.642
For all the people in this church, I would like to pray for you.

1168
02:04:55.642 --> 02:04:57.642
Perhaps we can close our eyes.

1169
02:04:57.642 --> 02:05:02.642
I really want to conclude this sermon.

1170
02:05:03.642 --> 02:05:11.642
And I really want to knock on your heart at this moment,

1171
02:05:11.642 --> 02:05:18.642
all the people in the church, including those who are currently locked up.

1172
02:05:18.642 --> 02:05:25.642
Also those who refuse to raise their hands for King Jesus ever.

1173
02:05:25.642 --> 02:05:28.642
If you are too stubborn to do that in an open church,

1174
02:05:28.642 --> 02:05:30.642
for I will not do that when they say so,

1175
02:05:30.642 --> 02:05:33.642
that is up to you. That is not my problem.

1176
02:05:33.642 --> 02:05:37.642
But then do it in your own room. Desire it there instead.

1177
02:05:37.642 --> 02:05:40.642
Acknowledge Jesus.

1178
02:05:40.642 --> 02:05:44.642
I want to pray for you and I also want to warn you,

1179
02:05:44.642 --> 02:05:49.642
dear brother or sister, if you know of yourself that you are stubborn,

1180
02:05:49.642 --> 02:05:52.642
break your own stubbornness.

1181
02:05:52.642 --> 02:05:55.642
The authority is upon yourself.

1182
02:05:55.642 --> 02:06:00.642
You can humble yourself before Jesus.

1183
02:06:00.642 --> 02:06:02.642
And he asks it of you.

1184
02:06:02.642 --> 02:06:05.642
If you hold on to a certain sin,

1185
02:06:05.642 --> 02:06:09.642
I truly want to warn you in the name of Jesus.

1186
02:06:09.642 --> 02:06:12.642
Give yourself to King Jesus.

1187
02:06:12.642 --> 02:06:15.642
Repent of your stubbornness.

1188
02:06:15.642 --> 02:06:17.642
Be humble of heart.

1189
02:06:17.642 --> 02:06:19.642
Come to the Lord.

1190
02:06:19.642 --> 02:06:21.642
Recognize him.

1191
02:06:21.642 --> 02:06:24.642
Start to acknowledge him as Jesus.

1192
02:06:24.642 --> 02:06:26.642
As King.

1193
02:06:26.642 --> 02:06:29.642
Maybe you say yes, but Tim, I have experienced this or that,

1194
02:06:29.642 --> 02:06:32.642
and I have seen this and that, I can no longer.

1195
02:06:32.642 --> 02:06:36.642
Here is my encouragement. You can do it.

1196
02:06:36.642 --> 02:06:40.642
Dear brother, dear sister, you can do it.

1197
02:06:40.642 --> 02:06:43.642
You can give yourself to God.

1198
02:06:43.642 --> 02:06:46.642
You can be in your secret inner room,

1199
02:06:46.642 --> 02:06:48.642
for that is where Jesus prefers it most.

1200
02:06:48.642 --> 02:06:52.642
He prefers that you bow your knees before King Jesus,

1201
02:06:52.642 --> 02:06:56.642
when you are alone. Then do not do it in open church as a show.

1202
02:06:56.642 --> 02:06:59.642
If you see it as a show, then do not do it yet.

1203
02:06:59.642 --> 02:07:02.642
But start in your own room.

1204
02:07:02.642 --> 02:07:05.642
Holy Spirit, help us as a church.

1205
02:07:05.642 --> 02:07:08.642
Help us to be humble of heart.

1206
02:07:08.642 --> 02:07:11.642
Lord, I want to bless everyone,

1207
02:07:11.642 --> 02:07:15.642
who has truly been able to take great steps with King Jesus,

1208
02:07:15.642 --> 02:07:18.642
by putting aside that carnal desire,

1209
02:07:18.642 --> 02:07:21.642
by the things that are destructive to our body,

1210
02:07:21.642 --> 02:07:24.642
by truly giving up that sin, and then we walk in freedom.

1211
02:07:24.642 --> 02:07:28.642
Lord, I want to thank you for those people who are already walking in that freedom.

1212
02:07:28.642 --> 02:07:33.642
Bless us then, Holy Spirit, with the instruction of humility,

1213
02:07:33.642 --> 02:07:39.642
so that we can always look at other people in the church or on the street with love.

1214
02:07:39.642 --> 02:07:43.642
Lord, help us to have the love of Jesus.

1215
02:07:43.642 --> 02:07:48.642
Jesus, inspire us with your humility.

1216
02:07:48.642 --> 02:07:53.642
For those people who are suffering with the long 'ij' in open church,

1217
02:07:53.642 --> 02:07:56.642
I want to bless you and I want to encourage you,

1218
02:07:56.642 --> 02:08:00.642
please wait for the righteousness of God.

1219
02:08:00.642 --> 02:08:03.642
For He is coming. He is trustworthy.

1220
02:08:03.642 --> 02:08:07.642
He gives it in His time and in His way.

1221
02:08:07.642 --> 02:08:11.642
But trust the Lord. Trust the Lord.

1222
02:08:11.642 --> 02:08:15.642
Trust the Lord when you go through difficult situations.

1223
02:08:15.642 --> 02:08:19.642
Trust the Lord when you are not having it easy in life.

1224
02:08:19.642 --> 02:08:24.642
Trust the Lord, for your suffering at this moment

1225
02:08:24.642 --> 02:08:29.642
will ultimately lead to a reward if you hold on to Him.

1226
02:08:29.642 --> 02:08:33.642
In Jesus' mighty name. And we all say amen.

1227
02:08:33.642 --> 02:08:35.642
Shall we give Jesus a round of applause?

1228
02:08:38.642 --> 02:08:42.642
Praise God. Dear people, tomorrow there is prayer.

1229
02:08:42.642 --> 02:08:46.642
And... What? Amen. For sure, amen.

1230
02:08:46.642 --> 02:08:51.642
Tomorrow there is prayer. And I would say, enjoy this Sunday.

1231
02:08:51.642 --> 02:08:56.642
Have a nice snowball fight with each other if there is still snow outside.

1232
02:08:56.642 --> 02:09:01.642
But be blessed in the name of Jesus. Amen? Amen. Bye-bye.
